1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,288
My shadow just walked away from my feet and left an eviction notice taped to the pavement.

2
00:00:06,588 --> 00:00:14,340
I chased it down three neon-drenched blocks, but it moved faster than any normal human silhouette could.

3
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:21,792
It stopped outside a towering glass bank, sliding right under the heavy doors like spilled black ink.

4
00:00:22,092 --> 00:00:29,508
I slipped inside behind a midnight clerk and found my shadow standing at a glowing ATM machine.

5
00:00:29,808 --> 00:00:37,248
The screen flashed red with a staggering balance. Seven years of ground-rent, billed directly to my feet.

6
00:00:37,548 --> 00:00:44,460
That is when the dark shape turned around, revealing it had my face carved into its chest.

7
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:50,928
It whispered that without its daily payments to the city core, my feet would lose their grip.

8
00:00:51,228 --> 00:00:58,740
Gravity isn't a natural law here. It is a subscription service, and my account is currently overdrawn.

9
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:06,600
My heels floated upward into the empty air, untethered and weightless inside the silent bank vault.

10
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:12,924
If I stop paying today, do I finally get to fly, or do I simply vanish?
